      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1867 Deansboro Railroad Station carried the Utica, Clinton and Binghamton line until 1957 and earned a National Register spot in 2002.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/deansboro_new_york",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Built in 1867, the station was the first board‑and‑batten depot on the line and opened for regular service on January 6, 1868 with James Hanchett as agent.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
